<div class="main ts-contain cf right-sidebar">
<div class="the-post-header s-head-modern s-head-large">
<div class="post-meta post-meta-a post-meta-left post-meta-single has-below"><div class="post-meta-items meta-above"><span class="meta-item cat-labels">
<a href="https://indiegame.com/en/archives/category/recommendation-public" class="category term-color-184" rel="category">Recommendation/Promotion</a>
</span>
</div><h1 class="is-title post-title">Banana Airways Lands in Steam Next Fest’s Top 25: Buenos Aires Duo’s 6-Player Co-op Flight Attendant Chaos Sim Targets Q1 2027</h1><div class="post-meta-items meta-below"><span class="meta-item post-author"><span class="by">By</span> <a href="https://indiegame.com/en/archives/author/desk" title="Posts by Editorial Team" rel="author">Editorial Team</a></span><span class="meta-item date"><time class="post-date" datetime="2026-10-26T15:09:16+09:00">2026년 10월 26일</time></span><span class="meta-item has-next-icon date-modified"><span class="updated-on">Updated:</span><time class="post-date" datetime="2026-10-27T13:58:50+09:00">2026년 10월 27일</time></span><span class="meta-item read-time has-icon"><i class="tsi tsi-clock"></i>5 Mins Read</span></div></div></div>
<div class="ts-row">
<div class="col-8 main-content">
<div class="the-post s-post-large">
<article id="post-38653" class="post-38653 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail category-recommendation-public">
<div class="post-content-wrap">
<div class="post-content cf entry-content content-spacious">
<p>Serve the coffee. Quarantine the radioactive passenger. Crawl out onto the wing to fix the burning engine. And whatever you do, don’t let the baby reach the cockpit. <em>Banana Airways</em> has made a strong first impression on players worldwide, emerging as one of the next co-op games to watch.</p>
<p><em>Banana Airways</em>, a co-op comedy game co-developed by Eggscape Entertainment and 3dar, ranked among the top 25 demos by concurrent players during Steam Next Fest.</p>
<p>In <em>Banana Airways</em>, one to six players take on the role of flight attendants who must get passengers safely to their destination while dealing with all manner of absurd, randomly occurring in-flight disasters.</p>
<p>The game is being developed by two talented studios from Buenos Aires, Argentina, and stands out for its friendship-testing comedy amid the chaos of a plane in total disarray.</p>
<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe loading="lazy" title="Banana Airways - Official Trailer" width="788" height="443" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/S0zY4Ub1lyY?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<h3>From Hungry Passengers to Burning Engines: It’s All the Crew’s Job</h3>
<p>As flight attendants, players hustle to hand out in-flight meals to hungry passengers while also quarantining and treating passengers exposed to radiation, with barely a moment to breathe.</p>
<p>The job doesn’t stop at the cabin door. You may need to crawl out onto the wing mid-flight to repair a broken engine, or plug a hole in the fuselage with your own body. Leave a hole unpatched too long, and part of the cabin gets sucked out into the open sky.</p>
<p>There’s more chaos on board. Radioactive chickens that might explode at any moment and hungry livestock roam the cabin, and you’ll also have to tend to a baby that won’t stop crying. Ignore the baby, and it may crawl into the cockpit, grab the controls, and start flying the plane.</p>
<p>You can tackle the chaotic flight solo or invite up to five friends to handle it together as a crew of six. “Rather than recreating a realistic flight sim, we focused on the joy of pure chaos: scrambling with your friends to keep a plane in total disarray together,” the developers said.</p>
<div id="jgb-slideshow-1" class="wp-block-jetpack-slideshow jgb-slideshow aligncenter" data-autoplay="false" data-delay="3000" data-effect="slide"><div class="swiper jgb-slideshow__swiper"><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_1-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_2-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_3-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div><div class="swiper-button-prev"></div><div class="swiper-button-next"></div></div></div>
<h3>Co-op Crisis Management and Physics Comedy</h3>
<p>The developers highlight two key features: co-op play in which disasters erupt everywhere at once, and physics-based comedy.</p>
<p>When severe turbulence hits, characters flop around like ragdolls, and players still have to keep serving hot coffee while engines burn and radioactive passengers run wild.</p>
<p>On top of that, ticking time bombs and real-time structural damage keep throwing outlandish crises at players without letup.</p>
<div id="jgb-slideshow-2" class="wp-block-jetpack-slideshow jgb-slideshow aligncenter" data-autoplay="false" data-delay="3000" data-effect="slide"><div class="swiper jgb-slideshow__swiper"><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_4-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_5-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_6-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div><div class="swiper-button-prev"></div><div class="swiper-button-next"></div></div></div>
<h3>Cartoon 3D, First-Person View, and 31 Languages</h3>
<p>According to the Steam store page, physics-based gameplay and comedy are at the core, alongside cartoon-style graphics, vibrant colors, and an immersive first-person view. Built on Unity 6, it also boasts clean, optimized visuals.</p>
<p>Localization is extensive. <em>Banana Airways</em> will support 31 languages, including English, Spanish, Korean, Japanese, and Simplified and Traditional Chinese, so players around the world can enjoy the chaotic flight without a language barrier.</p>
<div id="jgb-slideshow-3" class="wp-block-jetpack-slideshow jgb-slideshow aligncenter" data-autoplay="false" data-delay="3000" data-effect="slide"><div class="swiper jgb-slideshow__swiper"><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_9-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_8-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_7-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div><div class="swiper-button-prev"></div><div class="swiper-button-next"></div></div></div>
<h3>Two Buenos Aires Studios, With Consoles in the Works</h3>
<p><em>Banana Airways</em> is co-developed by Eggscape Entertainment Inc. and 3dar, both based in Buenos Aires, Argentina, with publishing handled by Eggscape Entertainment.</p>
<p>PC via Steam is the only officially announced platform, but <strong>console versions are also planned</strong>. Specific consoles and release dates will be announced later.</p>
<div id="jgb-slideshow-4" class="wp-block-jetpack-slideshow jgb-slideshow aligncenter" data-autoplay="false" data-delay="3000" data-effect="slide"><div class="swiper jgb-slideshow__swiper"><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_12-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_11-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_10-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div><div class="swiper-button-prev"></div><div class="swiper-button-next"></div></div></div>
<h3>Top 25 by Concurrent Players</h3>
<p>The developers announced that shortly after Steam Next Fest began, the demo entered the top 25 by concurrent players.</p>
<p>The exact timing of the ranking, player counts, Steam user reviews, and wishlist numbers weren’t disclosed, but breaking into the top tier among a crowded field of indie titles is a notable early win.</p>
<p>Recalling the absurd moments from the trailer, such as chickens eating each other in the cabin and a baby seizing the controls, Eggscape Entertainment said: “We can’t wait to hear what you thought of your flight in the demo, so send us your impressions and feedback.”</p>
<p>The free demo was available throughout Steam Next Fest, which ran until October 26.</p>
<div id="jgb-slideshow-5" class="wp-block-jetpack-slideshow jgb-slideshow aligncenter" data-autoplay="false" data-delay="3000" data-effect="slide"><div class="swiper jgb-slideshow__swiper"><div class="swiper-wrapper"><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_16-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_14-1024x576.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="swiper-slide"><figure class="jgb-slideshow__slide"><img src="https://indiegame.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Banana-Airways_13-1024x572.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="swiper-pagination"></div><div class="swiper-button-prev"></div><div class="swiper-button-next"></div></div></div>
<h3>Who This Is For</h3>
<p>Strong fit for: friend groups who love chaotic co-op games like <em>Overcooked</em> or <em>Lethal Company</em>; fans of physics comedy and ragdoll mayhem; players who enjoy frantic multitasking; groups of up to six looking for something larger than the usual four-player co-op.</p>
<p>Less ideal for: players seeking a realistic flight or management sim; this is deliberately absurd.</p>
<h3>What to Watch For</h3>
<p>Next steps include pricing, the console platform announcement, and whether Eggscape shares wishlist figures after its Next Fest success. With a Q1 2027 target, feedback from the demo will likely shape the final build.</p>
<h3>The Takeaway</h3>
<p><em>Banana Airways</em> takes the familiar co-op formula of overlapping crises and sends it to 30,000 feet, complete with radioactive chickens, fuselage holes, wing-walking repairs, and a baby who really wants to fly the plane. A top-25 Next Fest showing, six-player co-op, and 31 languages give this Buenos Aires collaboration real momentum heading into 2027.</p>
<p>Release: Q1 2027 on Steam; consoles to follow.</p>
<hr class="wp-block-separator"/>
<h5>Information regarding &#8216;Banana Airways&#8217;</h5>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">item</th><th scope="col"> detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Developer</td><td> Eggscape Entertainment Inc., 3dar</td></tr><tr><td> Publisher</td><td> Eggscape Entertainment Inc. (Self-publishing)</td></tr><tr><td> Genre</td><td> Cooperative comedy, physics-based simulation, indie</td></tr><tr><td> platform</td><td> PC (Steam, Windows), Console (Specific platform TBD)</td></tr><tr><td> Player count</td><td> Single-player, Online co-op up to 6 players</td></tr><tr><td> Release date</td><td> Q1 2027</td></tr><tr><td> price</td><td> Unreleased</td></tr><tr><td> language</td><td> 31 languages including English, Spanish, Korean, and Japanese (Interface, audio, and subtitle distinctions unconfirmed)</td></tr><tr><td> Reactions/Evaluations</td><td> Top 25 Steam Next Fest Demos by Concurrent Users (Announced by Developers)</td></tr><tr><td> Steam Page</td><td> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4835560/Banana_Airways/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Shortcut</a></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
</div>
</div>
</article>
